<!--
  The gear glyph inside the 40x40 header entry control (G1).

  The control itself is unchanged - same 40x40 circle at x=334,y=12 in the 390x64
  band, same three headers, same `bg_settings_entry` plate. Only what it means
  changed: it opens `settings`, and `Settings > Профиль` is now how the profile is
  reached. See `docs/SETTINGS-APPEARANCE-3.6.6.md` for why that is the design's
  own structure rather than a new arrangement - the frozen `settings` frame draws
  Профиль as its first row.

  The frozen headers place a 16x16 icon container at x=12,y=12 inside the 40x40
  circle, so the viewport here is the whole circle and the glyph occupies 12..28
  within it - the same contract `ic_settings_entry` was drawn to, which is why the
  ImageView still carries no padding.

  The 16x16 placement is expressed as a group transform over a 24-unit path rather
  than as re-projected coordinates: 24 * (2/3) = 16, then translated by 12, so the
  numbers in the transform are the ones the frame states and can be checked
  against it. A VectorDrawable group applies scale before translate, which is what
  makes that read in that order.

  `fillColor` is a colour resource rather than an `app:tint`, so values-night
  swaps it with no code - the rule the whole 3.6.6 icon set follows.
-->
